Improved handling of `WP_Query::getPosts()` when post name have been set as a wrong `query_var[name]` parameter. Before this url like http://localhost:8889/2026/10/05/[/ returns drafted post (if it was in DB). Now it will be return Not Found page.
There can be approach without changing `sanitize_title_for_query` function, but I think current approach is more clear. The second one: 
```
if ( '' !== $query_vars['name'] ) {
    $query_vars['name'] = sanitize_title_for_query( $query_vars['name']); 
    if ( '' !== $query_vars['name'] ) {
        $where .= " AND {$wpdb->posts}.post_name = '" . $query_vars['name'] . "'";
    } else {
       $where .= " AND {$wpdb->posts}.post_name LIKE ' '";
    }
} elseif {...
```
So it could be changed, if community minds

