Alternative to https://github.com/WordPress/wordpress-develop/pull/13806

This PR applies the user's admin color scheme to the admin bar on the front end.

## Approach

- `admin-bar.css` now reads its colors from custom properties, falling back to the current default colors.
- Each core color scheme only provides a small CSS block that sets those properties.
- In the admin screens, that block is part of the scheme's `colors.css`. On the front end, it is inlined.

Compared to the linked PR, this alternative does NOT add any new CSS request. `admin-bar.css` is already loaded currently, and no new public function or style handle is added.

### Addition to `colors.css`

Each scheme's `colors.css` no longer contains its own admin bar rules. Instead, it sets the custom properties. For example, in `colors/blue/colors.css`:

```css
#wpadminbar {
  --wp-admin--admin-bar--text: #fff;
  --wp-admin--admin-bar--background: #245278;
  --wp-admin--admin-bar--icon: #e5f8ff;
  --wp-admin--admin-bar--focus-text: #fff;
  --wp-admin--admin-bar--submenu-text: #e2ecf1;
  --wp-admin--admin-bar--submenu-background: rgb(27.7615384615, 63.2346153846, 92.5384615385);
  /* …6 more */
}
```

`admin-bar.css` then consumes them:

```css
#wpadminbar {
	background: var(--wp-admin--admin-bar--background, #1d2327);
}
```

### Inline style on the front end

`colors.css` is not loaded on the front end, so the same block is built into a separate `colors/{scheme}/admin-bar.css` file. Its contents are read on the server and attached to the existing `admin-bar` style handle:

```html
<style id="admin-bar-inline-css">
#wpadminbar{--wp-admin--admin-bar--text:#fff;--wp-admin--admin-bar--background:#245278;--wp-admin--admin-bar--icon:#e5f8ff;/* … */}
</style>
```

For the Fresh scheme and for color schemes registered by plugins, nothing is inlined, and the admin bar keeps its default colors.

## Trade-offs

Plugins might treat the custom property names introduced here (`--wp-admin--admin-bar--*`) as public, which would make them harder to rename or remove later. I believe, the current "direction" is to use WPDS tokens (`--wpds-*`)?

## Use of AI Tools

Used Claude Opus 5.5 to explore the approach and implement the changes.
